+*C-score +2*
+
+```text
+For certain routines (namely, "abs", "ceil", and "strlen"), the front end will
+create an implicit alias between these routines and their corresponding
+builtin counterparts and then fold calls to these routines when applicable.
+G++ (but not gcc or clang) apparently doesn't create an implicit alias when
+the routine has a definition.  The front end now emulates that.  For example:
