+accepted "#pragma weak ..." constructs, but just passed them through to the
+back end.  The front end otherwise ignored the #pragma, in particular during
+constant evaluation.  Now, in GCC and Clang compatibility modes, entities with
+C linkage matching a "#pragma weak <c_name>" directive (where <c_name> is the
+identifier naming the C-linkage entity) have their a_routine::is_weak or
+a_variable::is_weak flag set to TRUE, and that affects address comparisons
+during constant evaluation.  For example, in GNU C mode:
+
