+different B objects, however: The first refers to the subobject B of the D
+object being initialized whereas the second refers to the temporary object
+produced by the cast itself.  The two can be distinguished by the flag
+"implicit_aggr_element" in the constant entries representing the various
+data member initializers (the flag is FALSE for "this->x+2" but TRUE for
+"this->x+1" in the expanded aggregate initializer).
