+## 2016-09-02 · `EDGcpfe/17503`
+
+**Bit fields in IL entries**
+
+*C-score +6*
+
+```text
+Bit fields in IL entries are always declared with type a_bit_field.  When
+building the front end with a Microsoft compiler a_bit_field was previously
+a typedef for "unsigned char" to allow for more compact layouts of some IL
+entries.  That is, however, not always sufficient to hold bit fields
+representing type qualifier sets (and, theoretically, large name
+linkage sets), particularly with the recent addition of the C11 _Atomic
+qualifier and the Clang nullability qualifiers.  a_bit_field is now always
+a typedef for "unsigned int".  To mitigate the potential increase in memory
+usage by front ends built with a Microsoft compiler, a few changes were made
+to some types (in particular, the "kind" field of an_expr_node is now a bit
+field).
