+```text
+A new configuration macro, USE_HEX_FP_CONSTANTS_IN_GENERATED_CODE, has been
+introduced to control whether floating-point values should be emitted as
+hexadecimal floating-point constants (when the macro is TRUE), or as they had
+been, as decimal floating-point constants (when the macro is FALSE) in
+generated code.  Using hexadecimal floating-point constants has the advantage
+of requiring one less floating-point to decimal conversion in the front end
+and one less decimal to floating-point conversion by the back end (thereby
+increasing the likelihood that the floating-point value internally
+represented in the front end is the value that is used at run-time).
