+with "static" in the file scope).  Previously, such declarations were handled
+identically in GNU C modes.  Now, when gnu_version >= 40000, such declarations
+trigger an error, and when gnu_version < 30400, the "static" specifier is
+ignored (in the example above, this results in f having external linkage).
