+**IA-64 ABI: Set least significant bit in guard when using ARM EABI (affects ARM in big-endian mode)**
+
+*C-score +2*
+
+```text
+The IA-64 ABI uses the first byte of a guard variable to protect one-time
+initialization of static data (see section 2.8 of the IA-64 ABI).
+The ARM EABI differs in that the least significant bit of the guard variable
+is used to protect the one-time initialization (see section 4.4.2 of the ARM
+EABI).  Previously, with IA64_ABI_USE_INT_STATIC_INIT_GUARD set to TRUE
+(i.e., use ARM EABI semantics for static guards), the front end generated
+guard test queried the least significant bit, but set the first byte once the
