+In GNU C mode, such a member can be any field of the struct (not just the last
+one).  When both GNU C and C99 extensions were enabled, the front end used to
+require the tighter constraints of plain (nonstrict) C99 mode.  Now the
+broader GNU C mode extension is accepted.  For example:
