+## 2003-11-23
+
+**In C99, & followed by * cancels out**
+
+*C-score +3*
+
+```text
+According to section 6.5.3.2 of the C99 standard, a "&" operator
+over a "*" operator cancels out both, so something like "&*x"
+is equivalent to "x".  This is significant when "x" is a pointer
+to void, because "*x" in that case is not an lvalue.  The
+cancellation is now implemented.
+
+In a related tweak, the end position on the operand for "*x"
+in the above is now correct.  Formerly, it was one column too
+high.
+```
