+mode incorrectly considered the temporary created a short-lifetime
+temporary.  Though the C++ standard doesn't have compound literals
+and therefore doesn't offer guidance on the lifetime of such temporaries,
+the C99 standard says that local compound literals survive to
+end of block, so we have changed to that interpretation.  The
+former approach also caused a bug: two compound literals of the
+same type in the same block used the same temporary, but of
+course the temporary could be initialized to only one of the
+compound literals, so the other use got the wrong value.
+Now fixed.
