+## 2002-06-18
+
+**GNU C compatibility: Redefinition of extern __inline__ function**
+
+*C-score +4*
+
+```text
+In GNU C mode, a "extern __inline__" function definition can be followed
+by another definition of that function (a warning is issued).  The earlier
+definition is discarded and replaced by the latest one. For example:
+
+  extern __inline__ int f() { return 3; }  // No out-of-line copy
+  int f() { return 3; }                    // Out-of-line copy
+
+A call to the function may appear between two such definitions; if that
+call is inlined (by the lowering process), the first definition will be
+used for that purpose.  [Patch sent out 7/23/02.]
+```
