+```text
+In some European character sets, some of the character positions for
+C punctuation are assigned to alphabetic characters.  For example,
+in some German character sets the character position that is ASCII "]"
+is "U umlaut".  That means once the setlocale call has been done, "]"
+suddenly looks like an identifier character, which causes many strange
+errors.  We have changed the initialization of the is_id_char array
+to ensure that the problem characters, i.e.,
+
+ [ \ ] ^ { | } ~
+
